.TITLE "sudo"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Allows a permitted user to execute a command as the __superuser__ or another user. It is the standard way to perform __administrative tasks__ securely.

.DIV "TLDR"
**sudo command**
Executes a specific command with administrative (root) privileges.
> __command__ the tool to run

**sudo -u user command**
Runs a command as a specific user instead of the root user.
> __-u__ user flag | __user__ the target username | __command__ tool to run

**sudo -i**
Opens an interactive login shell with root privileges.
> __-i__ interactive login flag

**sudo -l**
Lists the permissions and commands allowed for the current user.
> __-l__ list permissions flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __sudo__ is safer than logging in as root because it maintains an audit trail of administrative actions. Always verify the command you are running, as mistakes made with __sudo__ can have system-wide consequences.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:whoami**

documentation: __https://www.sudo.ws/man/1.8.15/sudo.man.html__
